WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:06.195
Europa or Jupiter II is the smallest and least massive of Jupiter's four Galilean moons.

00:06.661 --> 00:14.687
It is observable from Earth with common binoculars and is a planetary-mass moon, slightly smaller and less massive than Earth's Moon.

00:15.196 --> 00:21.746
Europa is an icy moon, and, of the three icy Galilean moons, the closest orbiting Jupiter.

00:22.346 --> 00:27.224
As a result, it exhibits a relatively young surface shaped by tidal heating.
